.TITLE "tasklist"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays a list of currently running processes on the local computer or on a remote computer. It provides details such as process name, PID, and __memory usage__.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**tasklist**
Lists all currently running processes on the local machine.
> 

**tasklist /v**
Displays verbose information for each process.
> __/v__ verbose flag

**tasklist /svc**
Lists the services hosted in each process.
> __/svc__ services flag

**tasklist /fi "status eq running"**
Filters the list to show only running processes.
> __/fi__ filter flag | __"status eq running"__ the filter criteria

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __tasklist__ is the command-line equivalent of the Task Manager. It is useful for identifying background processes that may be consuming excessive system resources.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:taskkill** **windows:systeminfo**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/tasklist__
